<section>
  <section>
    <h2>Why does accessibility matter?</h2>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>As to not exclude anyone</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Market share</li>
      <li>Corporate social responsability</li>
      <li>Loyal customers</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Technical reasons</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>In line with general web standards</li>
      <li>Cross platform compatibility</li>
      <li>Responsive design</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Financial reasons</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Independant clients cost you less</li>
      <li>Increased search engine optimisation</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>To comply with the law</h2>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2 european directives</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Web Accessibility directive </strong>: websites and apps of
        public sector
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>European Accessibility Act </strong>: certain common products
        and services
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Web accessibility directive</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32016L2102&from=EN">
          Full text in Official Journal
        </a>{' '}
        (available in all EU languages)
      </li>
      <li>
        Websites and mobile applications maintained by public sector bodies must
        be accessible.
      </li>
      <li>They must publish an accessibility statement</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>European Accessibility act</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The Act came into force on 27 June 2019 and Member States have 3 years
        to transpose it into national law.
      </li>
      <li>Businesses will need to comply with the EAA by June 2025.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The products and services covered by the EAA include:</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>ATMs, ticketing and check-in machines, payment terminals</li>
      <li>banking services</li>
      <li>e-commerce</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Accessibility statement</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>What is the current level of accessibility?</li>
      <li>Which alternatives are provided?</li>
      <li>How can the visitor provide feedback?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The standard:</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (
        <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">WCAG 2.2</a>)
      </li>
      <li>
        For websites, mobile apps, digital documents, newsletters, Facebook
        posts ...
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>
